{"content":[{"c":["ABIJAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Samuel’s second son who, with his older brother, Joel, was a corrupt judge in Beersheba. Because of the corruption, Israel’s leaders demanded to be ruled instead by a king (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.8.2","r":"1Sam.8.2","rawR":"1Sam.8.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.8.2","value":"1Sam.8.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 8:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.28","r":"1Chr.6.28","rawR":"1Chr.6.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.28","value":"1Chr.6.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:28"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Son of Jeroboam I of the northern kingdom of Israel. The boy’s illness impelled his family to seek guidance from the prophet Ahijah at Shiloh (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.14.1-2","r":"1Kgs.14.1-2","rawR":"1Kgs.14.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.14.1-2","value":"1Kgs.14.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 14:1-2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Alternate name for Abijam, king of Judah, in ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.12.16-14.1","r":"2Chr.12.16-14.1","rawR":"2Chr.12.16-14.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.12.16-14.1","value":"2Chr.12.16-14.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chronicles 12:16–14:1"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.1.7","r":"Matt.1.7","rawR":"Matt.1.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.1.7","value":"Matt.1.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matthew 1:7"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Abijam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Abijam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Abijam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Abijam"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Ahaz’s wife, and mother of King Hezekiah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.18.2","r":"2Kgs.18.2","rawR":"2Kgs.18.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.18.2","value":"2Kgs.18.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 18:2"},", short form “Abi”; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.1","r":"2Chr.29.1","rawR":"2Chr.29.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.1","value":"2Chr.29.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 29:1"},"). This Abijah was Zechariah’s daughter."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Becher’s son from Benjamin’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.8","r":"1Chr.7.8","rawR":"1Chr.7.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.8","value":"1Chr.7.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Levite who headed the eighth of 24 priestly divisions established in David’s time (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.10","r":"1Chr.24.10","rawR":"1Chr.24.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.10","value":"1Chr.24.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 24:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.1.5","r":"Luke.1.5","rawR":"Luke.1.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.1.5","value":"Luke.1.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 1:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["7. Head of a priestly family who signed Ezra’s covenant of faithfulness to God with Nehemiah and others after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.7","r":"Neh.10.7","rawR":"Neh.10.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.7","value":"Neh.10.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["8. Head of a priestly family who returned to Jerusalem with Zerubbabel after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.4","r":"Neh.12.4","rawR":"Neh.12.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.4","value":"Neh.12.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:4"},"). Perhaps of the same family as #7."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Abijah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 8:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.8.2","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.8.2","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.8.2"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.28","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.28","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.28"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 14:1-2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.14.1-2","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.14.1-2","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.14.1-2"},{"ancho